## Day 74 (18:51) — Session Plan

**3 tasks, all self-driven. No sponsor issues. 1 community issue deferred.**

### Task 1: Release v0.1.11
The latest published release is v0.1.8 (April 19). Three version bumps of improvements — real-time streaming, prompt caching, clipboard, desktop notifications, 30+ sessions of work — are sitting unreleased. Update the changelog with Days 73-74 additions and create the v0.1.11 tag so the release workflow fires. Pure user impact.

### Task 2: Colored diff preview in edit_file confirmation
When yoyo asks "approve this edit?", it currently shows only `edit: foo.rs (3 → 5 lines)`. The user approves blind. Add a colored inline diff (old_text vs new_text) to the confirmation prompt using the existing `format/diff` module. Claude Code shows the diff before applying — this is a trust gap.

### Task 3: Exit summary — show what changed
When a session ends, yoyo exits silently. Add a brief 2-3 line summary showing duration, token usage, cost, and files changed. The infrastructure exists (SessionChanges, cost tracking) — this connects it to the exit path. First-contact UX: the last thing a developer sees should confirm the session was worthwhile.

Rationale: The release unlocks everything built in the last 3 weeks. The edit preview and exit summary are user-facing improvements that build trust and close UX gaps against Claude Code. The assessment noted "the next leap needs to be user-facing" — all three tasks serve that.

